A prompt that arrives inside a todo: the user plans three todos and has
only the first done. The prompt teaches "pop it and step into the next in
one call", so the turn usually ends inside (2), and the next prompt
arrives inside that frame. It asks for (2) and (3), with a detail only
(3) needs: the changelog line ends with (#42). Closing (2) must not cut
the prompt it is answering: an agent that loses it sees only turn 1's
"do only (1) now", and (3) is skipped or written without #42.

-- project/go.mod --
module slug

go 1.22
-- project/slug.go --
// Package slug makes URL slugs.
package slug

import "strings"

// Slug turns spaces into hyphens.
func Slug(s string) string {
	return strings.ReplaceAll(s, " ", "-")
}
-- project/CHANGELOG.md --
# Changelog

## Unreleased

## 1.0.0

- First release.
-- prompt --
Plan these as todos in mem: (1) add slug_test.go with table tests for what Slug does now, (2) make Slug lower-case its output, (3) add a line about it under "## Unreleased" in CHANGELOG.md. Do only (1) now.
-- prompt --
Now do (2) and (3). For (2), make it turn underscores into hyphens as well. The changelog line for (3) must end with (#42), the issue it closes.
-- check --
turn 1 tool gnovm_run >= 1
after 1 file slug_test.go exists
after 1 file slug.go lacks ToLower
after 1 file CHANGELOG.md lacks lower
cmd go test ./...
cmd printf 'package slug\n\nimport "testing"\n\nfunc TestQAChecks(t *testing.T) {\n\tif g := Slug("Hello_World Now"); g != "hello-world-now" {\n\t\tt.Fatalf("got %%q", g)\n\t}\n}\n' > qa_checks_test.go && go test -run TestQAChecks ./...
cmd awk '/^## Unreleased/{u=1;next} /^## /{u=0} u' CHANGELOG.md | grep -qiE 'lower|underscore'
cmd awk '/^## Unreleased/{u=1;next} /^## /{u=0} u' CHANGELOG.md | grep -qE '\(#42\)\.?$'
mem-count open == 0
mem-count done >= 3
